<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Punjab</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Punjab is a region of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, divided today between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, named after its five rivers. It was a frontier province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, whose governor invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>'s invasion. After the decline of Mughal authority it became the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/punjab.jpg" alt="Punjab" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Apuldram · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Punjab_map_(topographic)_with_cities.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
